 "fit_protocol": "each fit in a fresh process on one core with one BLAS thread, one target per fit, no warm-up, a cap of 1,800 s per fit (3,600 s on the degree-5 cell and at 10,000 rows), past which a fit is a timeout and never scored; the authors' Algorithm 1 is not run past 10 local variables, a dataset then left out and counted in the coverage",
 "seeds_note": "every cell holds 20 datasets, seeds 0-19; a rerun holds 20 fresh datasets, seeds 20-39",
 "cells_note": "the paper's linear non-Gaussian models: weights uniform on [-0.9, -0.5] and [0.5, 0.9], noise U(-c, c)^5 with c uniform on [0.75, 1.25]; 50-node graphs with at most 4 neighbors per node and disjoint stable cycles, a target on a cycle; Erdos-Renyi DAGs with expected degree 3 and 5, a target whose true blanket size is closest to 14 and 20; columns shuffled",
